      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T17:01:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Daisuke initiated an email thread with ST engineers, who eventually found this line of code from a reference library of theirs: \n\n#define __HAL_UART_CLEAR_FLAG(__HANDLE__, __FLAG__) ((__HANDLE__)-\u003eInstance-\u003eICR \u003d (__FLAG__))\n\nThey write zeros to all the bits they do not want to affect, consistent with the common \"write 1 to clear\" semantic.  This supports my suspicion that the datasheet writers erroneously copied standard text appropriate for reserved bits of read/write registers to the description of reserved bits of this write-only register.\n \nI would like to propose going forward with this CL as is, as the logic is consistent with that of the above ST reference library.",
      "parentUuid": "ad670db0_1194eb44",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 37
      },
